A||||13||Sage||ANOTHER SCOOP OPTION||||1||
Z||000000||Sage||08-24-2000||03:17 PM||||I noticed Rockcrawls scoops in another post and the bit about the Holley scoops on ebay, so thought I would let ya'll know that I have yet another option for those that maybe are a little more timid and would like to keep a little more of the original look.  It is based on the Holley style scoop, but is a little lower profile and is fiberglass and will take paint very well.  Am getting ready to make the mold very soon.  Have worked out a situation with Doug007 at the Fierowarehouse and they will be available thru him if anyone is interested.<P>Next on the agenda will be Meechum style panels that will replace the entire quarter panel. These will come finished in high grade gel coat and be ready to paint after sanding lightly with #400.  <P>Just thought I would put it out there to let you know.<P>Thanks for the space, and have good one!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/scoop1_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||08-24-2000||04:07 PM||||I'm not interested in the little scoop, but the thought of a Mecham style scoop of good quality for a reasonable price (hey-if it's going through Doug, it has to be reasonable) makes me drool.  Got any pics, prices, descriptions, etc???||||reg||1
Z||000002||Sage||08-26-2000||12:23 PM||||MM:<P>Sorry for the delay in responding to your questions, but could not connect for the last couple days, no clue as to why.<P>I have not decided on a final design for the side scoops yet.  Am open to ideas, suggestions, to help determine what most would want.  I do know that it will be a complete replacement panel.  Don't really want to just make another copy of the meechum scoops, but the varieties are somewhat limited as to what can be done without getting too extreme! <BR>Should it be ribbed?  Curvy or square? How far out do you want to get?<P>I figure they should go for around $100.00 a side, but that will be determined by the final design, and what Doug wants to sell them for.<P>Anyway, all input is welcomed.<P>As a footnote: The pic above(of the little scoop)is NOT the finished product.  It is a pic of a half finished "plug" the final is near completion and mold will follow shortly.<P>These little scoops will replace the finned plastic piece that comes on the car, and will use the original screws and mount exactly the same way.<P>Am toying with the idea of embossing "FIERO" on the center section in the same font as what is on the embossed v6 plenums.  What do you think, worth the effort?<P>Thanks for the space,  have a good one!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Xtreme Fiero's||08-26-2000||05:39 PM||||I you make it say "V6 Ram Air" i'll buy 1 if you make it say "Ram Air" i'll buy 8  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||007DOUG||08-26-2000||11:01 PM||||All I can say is, whatever Sage makes, IT WON'T BE JUNK. He knows everything, and can do anything when it comes to fiberglass. (Hey sage, show them some pics of the Bereatta ground FX's). And he's a damn good fiero painter too.<P>We need input as to what YOU want on your fiero. <P>Is this a good design for a "holley style" scoop? What do YOU want the side of the scoop to read?<P>Does everyone like the mecham style scoops? Or can they look even better?<P>As for price......I don't care if I make a dime. Fierp Parts are how I "unwind", they are my hobby. I already have three jobs, and don't want a forth. <P>SAGE NEEDS INPUT EVERYONE. THIS IS YOUR PROJECT TOO.<P>------------------<BR>4 Indy pace Cars<BR>84 T-top<BR>84 SE<BR>86 SE V6 153K<BR>2 86 GT's<BR>86 GT 3.4 Pearl White T-top<BR>2 88 GT twins<P>However......<BR><I>"Time is my most precious and most perishable of all my possessions."</I>||||reg||14
