Z||000010||rockcrawl||03-31-2001||09:33 PM||||My molds are complete and I'm ready to make the extractor vents for anyone who is interested. $125. each with screens. Unfortunately I don't have any pics of a painted hood yet. The truth is I don't own a Fiero at this point that I want to put one on. I've only got a stock '87 GT that I don't wanna mess with. Here's a link to a page with lots if installation pics and info. <A HREF="http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/extractorinstall.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/extractorinstall.htm</A> <BR> I also have the molds to make <B>exact</B> copies of the Mecham scoops, but my price is higher than FOCOA or Outlaw. The original Mecham scoops have been sold. I'm not making the small side scoops anymore.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Must be a better fit than the original Mechams<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>There is no such thing as a better fit than the originals. they were made of urethane and flexed just like the GM panels. they were smooth front and back and all edges were perfect. Holding them side by side with GM parts, you would think they were made in the GM factory. Not sure what happened to the original tooling for them, but it would be very valuable today.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Seanh||04-01-2001||01:00 AM||||Hey Rock, I really love those hood scoops, and really want a set, but I'm to unsure of myself to think I could do it myself. What do you think a body shop would charge to do it, and repaint my hood? I could probally do the cutting, mounting and glassing myself, but I don't know how difficult it is and if I could do it or not. Thanks||||reg||1
